# Public API compatibility baseline: 0.28.0 (the last published release; the next release is checked
# against it). Add exclusions here only for intentional removals, with a comment explaining each.
# After a release is published: raise the baseline in .github/workflows/api-compatibility.yml to that
# version and delete the exclusions below, which then describe changes the baseline already contains.
# SheetWriter (the package-private AbstractSheetWriter, now public) holds the column methods of ExcelWriter and
# ExcelSheetWriter, and every writer takes a Consumer<ColumnConfig<T>> as its column configurer; ExcelColumn.ExcelColumnBuilder
# is removed (style(CellStyle) moved to ColumnConfig). Source compatible for code that passes lambdas; code compiled
# against 0.28.0 must be recompiled.
io.github.dornol.excelkit.excel.ExcelWriter
io.github.dornol.excelkit.excel.ExcelSheetWriter
io.github.dornol.excelkit.excel.TemplateListWriter
io.github.dornol.excelkit.excel.ExcelColumn$ExcelColumnBuilder
# ReadOptions gained the uniqueKey component, so its canonical constructor has one more parameter (use ReaderOptions.Builder).
io.github.dornol.excelkit.core.read.ReadOptions
# ExcelValidation gained list(...)/dependentList(...) and can no longer be extended (its constructor is private); use the static factories.
io.github.dornol.excelkit.excel.ExcelValidation
# CsvHandler is no longer AutoCloseable (close() removed, TempResourceContainer no longer its superclass): a handler is written after
# the method that made it returns, so try-with-resources released it too early. Use discard().
io.github.dornol.excelkit.csv.CsvHandler
# ExcelWriteErrorPolicy moved to core as WriteErrorPolicy, shared by every writer; CsvWriter.failOnColumnError(boolean) became writeErrorPolicy(WriteErrorPolicy).
io.github.dornol.excelkit.excel.ExcelWriteErrorPolicy
io.github.dornol.excelkit.csv.CsvWriter#failOnColumnError(boolean)
# The schema builder's writeErrorPolicy(...) takes the shared WriteErrorPolicy.
io.github.dornol.excelkit.schema.ExcelKitSchema$Builder#writeErrorPolicy(io.github.dornol.excelkit.excel.ExcelWriteErrorPolicy)
# ExcelWriter.InitOptions and ExcelWorkbook.InitOptions became one top-level WorkbookInitOptions; the settings they share are WorkbookOptions.
io.github.dornol.excelkit.excel.ExcelWriter$InitOptions
io.github.dornol.excelkit.excel.ExcelWorkbook$InitOptions
# AbstractReadHandler takes one ReadSessionConfig instead of the supplier, mapper, validator, selected columns and ReadOptions as separate
# constructor parameters; its only subclasses are the final CSV and Excel handlers of this library.
io.github.dornol.excelkit.core.read.AbstractReadHandler
# SchemaColumn.writeConfigurer() is a Consumer<ColumnConfig<T>> now that ExcelColumn.ExcelColumnBuilder is gone.
io.github.dornol.excelkit.schema.ExcelKitSchema$SchemaColumn
